  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MVO-CREM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands embassy in Jakarta, Indonesia, RVO, CSR Netherlands (www.mvonederland.nl), CREM BV (see www.crem.nl), Sustainable Business Development BV, FENEDEX (Federation of Dutch Exporters) and the FNLI (Federation of Dutch Food Industries) have developed this proposal for the execution of two parallel projects.There are two projects to focus on. The first one aims to explore the possibilities of institutionalizing corporate social responsibility (CSR) in Indonesia. The objective is to shift the focus from charity to CSR as a business case while involving stakeholders from both Dutch and Indonesian backgrounds. The second project focuses on identifying strategies to encourage sustainable food consumption in Indonesia. The project also explores opportunities for the Dutch sustainable agri-food sector, including exporters and investors.More critical consumers can improve the general business climate in Indonesia. This specific project aims to be the first pilot within the larger objective of the first project. If Indonesian consumers demand more sustainable products, it could incentivize businesses to consider CSR as a business case.</narrative>
  </description>
